<section class="phero"><div class="phero-media"><img src="/assets/img/photos/flood-street.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/flood-street-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/flood-street.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="683" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/serving-delaware/">Serving Delaware</a></li><li aria-current="page">Seaford</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker">Western Sussex</p><h1>Insurance Appraiser in Seaford, DE</h1><p class="lede">Once known as the “Nylon Capital of the World” for its DuPont plant, Seaford sits on the Nanticoke River in western Sussex County, with older neighborhoods, new homes and farmland nearby.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-coral" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-line light" href="/start-your-review/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="hero-facts"><div><dt>County</dt><dd>Sussex County</dd></div><div><dt>Region</dt><dd>Western Sussex</dd></div><div><dt>Inspections</dt><dd>On site</dd></div></dl></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose"><div class="local-card"><div><h2 class="local-h">Seaford at a glance</h2><dl class="local-dl"><div><dt>County</dt><dd>Sussex County</dd></div><div><dt>Neighborhoods</dt><dd>downtown Seaford, the neighborhoods off Stein Highway, Blades and communities along the Nanticoke</dd></div><div><dt>Housing mix</dt><dd>Mid-century homes built for plant workers, older downtown homes, new subdivisions and riverfront properties</dd></div></dl></div><div><p class="local-k">Local claim risks</p><ul class="chips"><li>Severe storms</li><li>Hurricane remnants</li><li>River flooding</li><li>Tree damage</li><li>Frozen pipes</li></ul></div></div>

<h2>A river town with industrial roots</h2>
<p>Seaford grew around the DuPont nylon plant that opened in 1939, and many neighborhoods date from the decades that followed. Those mid-century homes now often have older roofs, original plumbing and electrical systems — common sources of claim disputes. Insurance appraisal in Seaford frequently involves homes of this era.</p>
<h2>The Nanticoke River</h2>
<p>The Nanticoke runs through Seaford and Blades toward the Chesapeake Bay. Riverfront properties have beautiful views and real flood exposure. When storms bring both wind and high water, we separate damage covered under homeowners policies from flood damage.</p>
<h2>Inland but not immune</h2>
<p>Western Sussex County is far from the ocean, but tropical systems tracking up the Delmarva Peninsula bring wind and heavy rain inland. Summer storms and the occasional tornado also cross the flat farmland around Seaford, Laurel and Bridgeville.</p>
<h2>What we see most</h2>
<ul>
<li>Roof and siding damage on mid-century homes</li>
<li>Tree damage in established neighborhoods</li>
<li>Water losses from aging plumbing</li>
<li>Riverfront wind and flood questions</li>
<li>Farm and commercial building claims</li>
</ul>

