<h2>Questions from Seaford property owners</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>My house is from the 1950s. Will code upgrades be covered?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Code upgrades are often covered up to a limit under ordinance-or-law coverage. We identify required upgrades and check your limit.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do you cover Laurel and Bridgeville?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. We cover all of western Sussex County.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is my Nanticoke riverfront home in a flood zone?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Many riverfront properties are. Check FEMA flood maps and your flood policy, and keep in mind homeowners policies usually exclude flood.</p></div></details></div>
